Package: bubblequiz
Title: Print, Scan and Auto-Mark Multiple-Choice Bubble Sheets
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Will", "Cornwell", email = "wcornwell@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Will Cornwell [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Will Cornwell <wcornwell@gmail.com>
Description: An end-to-end toolkit for paper multiple-choice quizzes. Define the
    quiz shape once in a YAML config, print shuffled QR-coded forms, and mark
    scanned sheets with local computer vision before scoring them against the
    version-aware answer key. Designed to be installed once and called from
    any course repository.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    yaml,
    readr,
    dplyr,
    tibble,
    pdftools,
    magick,
    qpdf,
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    optparse,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: pandoc, xelatex, poppler, ImageMagick, zbar
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
